{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1368198-how-does-each-splat-deal-with-radiation","id":1368198,"title":"How does each Splat deal with radiation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-15T18:49:25-08:00","id":1368198,"title":"How does each Splat deal with radiation?","content":"So for a upcoming project I am working I was wondering how each splat would deal with radiation? Like could a werewolf and vampire could just heal through it? Mage just shield it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T20:05:48-08:00","id":1368212,"title":"","content":"<i><b>First Edition</b> (Saturnine Night radiation rules):</i><br /> Radiation damage is dealt by rolling a dice pool that is resisted by Supernatural Tolerance + Stamina. More intense radiation sources deal lethal or aggravated damage with a dice bonus. Half of the successes on this roll are suffered as damage a few hours after exposure. A week later, the character no longer heals naturally, and suffers the other half of the damage, one point per day.<br /> Vampires suffer the second stage of radiation poisoning not as damage but as a taint on points of their stored Vitae. Tainted points have to be spent before untainted points, don't cause vitae addiction or the Vinculum, and can't be used for healing or Physical Augmentation.<br /> Werewolves don't lose their natural healing from radiation poisoning.<br /> Mages' healing spells still work through radiation poisoning, and conjunctional Life + Forces spells can cure the radiation poisoning itself. Presumably a mage who expected to risk radiation poisoning could use Forces shielding of some sort to prevent it from settling in.<br /> Prometheans in the second stage of radiation poisoning roll each day to avoid (not just postpone) that day's radiation damage.<br /> No crossover rules were published for Bound or mummies. I presume that Bound could still spend plasm to absorb lethal or aggravated radiation damage. They'd still take it, but only as bashing. I do not know whether I would have mummies lose their natural healing or not; either way, they would not lose their ability to seal the flesh.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Second Edition</b> (Night Horrors: The Tormented and Deviant: The Renegades radiation rules):</i><br /> Radiation damage is dealt unrolled, always bashing, and the character cannot heal naturally while exposed to it. More intense radiation sources deal damage sooner and more frequently.<br /> A Promethean's Azoth can withstand exposure longer before suffering damage, and treats radiation sources as less intense.<br /> Deviants enjoy no particular special protection from radiation.<br /> No crossover rules were published, leaving it a judgment call whether active or supernatural healing remains effective for a given creature type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T19:37:23-08:00","id":1369489,"title":"","content":"I use tilts to model radiation poisoning. Personal Environment Tilt, pretty much.<br /> <br /> Level 1-4. All dice pools reduced by Level. Every day, roll Level and take the successes as aggravated damage.<br /> At the end of each month, roll a die. Failure means it downgrades, success means no change.<br /> <br /> 50-100 rads is Level 1. You'll get sick and death is possible but not certain and will take months.<br /> <br /> 100-500 rads is Level 2. You'll hurt. Half of mortals will die within a month.<br /> <br /> 500-1000 rads is Level 3. Almost no one survived this. Death almost certain within a week.<br /> <br /> 1000+ rads is Level 4. Death is all but guaranteed.<br /> <br /> As for how splats deal with it, Mages can use Forces to prevent it or Life to downgrade it. Werewolves only take lethal damage (per WtF p94) and roll to downgrade every week instead of every month. Vampires only take lethal damage (VtR p90) and will need to feed like crazy to heal. I've never had a changeling exposed to radiation so I don't know what I'd do there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 02-25-2020, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T08:18:25-08:00","id":1369584,"title":"","content":"Traditionally, <i>badly</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar